WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
- You're a very successful
business woman now.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.660
So, your path was very unusual.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.870
So, how did this all start?

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.703
- Well, you know,

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:12.670
I grew up in a world where
women are less than, right?

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.470
I think the easiest way to
explain it is that from the time

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:21.000
a child is old enough to speak
until the day that they die,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.620
if you are a male, if you are
a boy, as you become a man,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.900
your entire life, you say, when
you wake up in the morning,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.930
you say, thank you God for giving me life.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.820
And then you say, thank you
God for not making me a woman.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.700
- What?

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.010
- Thank you, God, for
not making me a woman.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.460
- Like literally they say that like?

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.610
- Every day, from the day
they're old enough to speak.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.260
You see your son saying it,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.330
you watch your husband
saying it, your father.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.880
- How that must impact you
as a woman in that community?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.120
Wow, that's tough.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.480
Um, and wow,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.070
and you said your daughter
changed your life, right?

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.510
- My daughter, Miriam,
is the reason I'm alive.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.940
I mean, that's just the fact.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.710
- You said your daughter
changed your life as well.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.640
- Absolutely, she was born.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.210
I had to change me,
to, to fit my daughter.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.330
- So well, speaking back of your daughter,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.000
was there one moment
that kind of stuck out.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.887
- And I want her to be like y'all

00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:12.050
- Oh!

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.543
- She's watching y'all,
she's watching you.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.377
- And we, we want.

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:19.210
- She's watching y'all.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.043
- I know, and we also want you

00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:21.400
to be whoever you are deep in there.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.233
- That's the main thing.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:24.190
- Yeah that's, yeah that's
it be whoever you want to be.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.023
So, what did your daughters say?

00:01:25.023 --> 00:01:27.280
- So my daughters, really
the beginning of my story

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.270
and the person who helped me leave,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.940
because it was an eight year trajectory.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.910
And it started when
Miriam was five years old,

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.570
I have a daughter named Miriam.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.170
She was asking, well, I
would like to play ball.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.720
I want to, I want to play basketball.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.553
I want to do this.

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:44.510
I want to learn how to sing
and I want to play the guitar.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:48.270
And she was constantly said,
no, you can't dance in public

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.550
because a man might see
you and have bad thoughts.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:51.560
You can't sing in public

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.480
because a man might see
you and have bad thoughts.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.700
And my little five-year-old
turned to my husband

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.700
and she would say, but why
isn't that his responsibility?

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:03.790
My five-year-old.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.270
- Out of the mouth of babies, yeah.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.420
- And then for the first
time she gave me permission,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.950
because my entire life,
I thought I was bad.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.570
That it wasn't okay for me,

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.620
but you couldn't convince me
that my five-year-old was bad.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.230
And she was saying,
this doesn't make sense.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.190
Why can't men control themselves?

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.010
And by the way, thank you.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.453
Why can't men control themselves?

00:02:24.453 --> 00:02:25.286
Excuse me.

00:02:25.286 --> 00:02:26.630
(audience applause)

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.488
- And by the way, they can.

00:02:28.488 --> 00:02:29.380
- And they should.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.190
- Yes, they can, they can.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.030
- And so that was when I
started educating myself.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.620
It took me eight years
before I walked out the door.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:37.870
If I had stayed,

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.730
she would have been
married off at 18 or 19,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.820
like everyone else.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:41.653
- Yeah.

00:02:41.653 --> 00:02:42.670
- She certainly wouldn't be in college.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.560
She certainly wouldn't be a tech genius.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.841
- Well, she changed your
life and you changed hers.

00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:47.674
That's amazing.

00:02:47.674 --> 00:02:49.880
- I mean, we literally saved
each other, and you know?

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:50.713
- Wow.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.680
Okay, so what's your favorite
thing to do um, now that,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.530
You know, now that you would

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.900
have been forbidden to
do something before,

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.540
like what's your favorite thing to do?

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.460
- Dance.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.293
- Oh!

00:03:00.293 --> 00:03:01.126
- I do love to dance.

00:03:01.126 --> 00:03:01.959
I do love to dance.

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:02.792
- I love dancing.

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:03.625
- Yeah I love dancing.

00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:04.458
- Yes.

00:03:04.458 --> 00:03:06.420
- And so to be able to actually move,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.240
to just let go and dance
is something I really love.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.470
- I love that.

